  "title": "CFdagger v2 k=16 Profile I compiler output contract",
  "type": "object",
  "x-arithmetic-invariants": [
    "r<=y and public_input_K_coordinates+1<=n; n,y,r>=1",
    "Exactly accumulator_state, fresh_state_01..16, folded_output_state use A_st; carrier uses A_H; field_auxiliary uses A_aux.",
    "Each segment uses minimal ring padding: matrix_columns=ceil(encoded_bits/64), zero_padding_coefficients=64*matrix_columns-encoded_bits; all A_st uses have equal lengths and columns.",
    "Each segment_id occurs exactly once. accumulator_state and fresh_state_01..16 use A_st/input; folded_output_state uses A_st/post_cauchy_pre_field; carrier uses A_H/pre_cauchy; field_auxiliary uses A_aux/post_cauchy_pre_field.",
    "state encoded_bits=192*(n+y); carrier encoded_bits=3072*r; auxiliary encoded_bits=192*auxiliary_gate_K_values+auxiliary_scalar_bits.",
    "Segments, uncommitted fixed-one coordinate, and uncommitted zero padding exactly partition 2^20 coefficients.",
    "fixed_zero_coordinates_count equals disjoint zero ranges length including segment padding; all zero coordinates constrained once in L0.",
    "linear_rows_before_backend_padding=40973+fixed_zero_coordinates_count; after=before+320.",
    "constraint_count_padded=2^ceil(log2(max(1,constraint_count_unpadded))); sumcheck_rounds=log2(constraint_count_padded)<=30.",
    "All matrix dimensions, layout, and template row counts are independent of c; only public coefficient values depend on c.",
    "Operation counts use explicit units and scopes; no sum across different units; Q/B/U/J costs and sparse public transpose costs covered.",
    "resolved_dimensions fields are derived aliases: semantic_dimension_n=semantic.n; residual_dimension_y=semantic.y; bilinear_image_dimension_r=semantic.r; fixed_zero_coordinates_count=handoff.fixed_zero_coordinates_count; sumcheck_rounds=r1cs.sumcheck_rounds; per-role columns and honest bounds equal the corresponding segment formulas. They must never be independent inputs.",
    "Before accepting COMPLETE, verify compiler and Q/U/J artifact SHA256 values, verify the exact A/B/C R1CS artifact set and their SHA256 values, and require every source_bit_mapping_artifact, wire_to_bit_coordinate_map_artifact and operation derivation_artifact to exist. Counts come from the emitted compiler artifacts; a COMPLETE tag alone is not evidence of circuit correctness.",
    "parameter_id and parameter_file_sha256 bind the exact selected parameters.json bytes, including source/carrier coordinate order, base-coefficient and bit order, and sumcheck point/table convention. The compiler must implement those conventions; hashes are not substitutes for checking them."
  ]
}
